d to load library\");\n        let func: Symbol<CpInflateFn> = lib.get(b\"cp_inflate\").expect(\"missing cp_inflate\");\n        let mut input = in_data.to_vec();\n        let mut output = vec![0u8; out_size];\n        let result = func(\n            input.as_mut_ptr() as *mut std::ffi::c_void,\n            input.len() as c_int,\n            output.as_mut_ptr() as *mut std::ffi::c_void,\n            output.len() as c_int,\n        );\n        if result == 0 {\n            None\n        } else {\n            Some(output)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn test_cp_inflate_simple() {\n    // A trivial fixed Huffman block: just an end-of-block code (256).\n    // In fixed Huffman tables, code 256 is encoded as 7 bits 0000000.\n    // Block header: BFINAL=1, BTYPE=01 (fixed) => bits 1, 01\n    // Bits emitted little-endian: bfinal=1 (bit 0), btype=01 (bits 1,2 = 1,0)\n    // EOB code 0000000 (7 bits, code value 0 reversed). Actually fixed Huffman\n    // code for symbol 256 is 7 bits, value 0. Reverse of 0 is 0. So 7 zero bits.\n    // First byte: bfinal=1, btype low=1, btype high=0, then 5 zero bits = 0b00000011 = 0x03\n    // That gives us 8 bits total: bfinal+btype = 3 bits, then 5 of the 7 EOB bits\n    // remaining 2 bits (zero) in next byte: 0x00\n    let input = vec![0x03, 0x00];\n    let c_result = unsafe { call_cp_inflate(C_LIB, &input, 0) };\n    let rust_result = unsafe { call_cp_inflate(RUST_LIB, &input, 0) };\n    assert_eq!(c_result.is_some(), rust_result.is_some());\n    if let (Some(c), Some(r)) = (c_result, rust_result) {\n        assert_eq!(c, r);\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn test_cp_inflate_uncompressed_block() {\n    // An uncompressed (stored) block containing \"Hello\"\n    // Block header: BFINAL=1, BTYPE=00\n    // Pad to byte, then LEN (16 bits), NLEN (~LEN, 16 bits), then data\n    let payload = b\"Hello\";\n    let len: u16 = payload.len() as u16;\n    let nlen: u16 = !len;\n    let mut input: Vec<u8> = vec![0x01]; // bfinal=1, btype=00\n    input.push((len & 0xff) as u8);\n    input.push((len >> 8) as u8);\n    input.push((nlen & 0xff) as u8);\n    input.push((nlen >> 8) as u8);\n    input.extend_from_slice(payload);\n    let c_result = unsafe { call_cp_inflate(C_LIB, &input, payload.len()) };\n    let rust_result = unsafe { call_cp_inflate(RUST_LIB, &input, payload.len()) };\n    assert_eq!(c_result.is_some(), rust_result.is_some());\n    if let (Some(c), Some(r)) = (c_result, rust_result) {\n        assert_eq!(c, r);\n        assert_eq!(&c[..], payload);\n    }\n}\n\n// Use libc crate for free\nmod libc {\n    use std::os::raw::c_void;\n    extern \"C\" {\n        pub fn free(ptr: *mut c_void);\n    }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
